# ryle-expository decontamination — 2026-08-12

Owner ruling 2026-08-12: "the lords garden, get it fixed" (taken as explicit go for both dev
and prod — the contamination was served user-facing on prod; a dev-only fix fixes nothing).

## Root cause (measured, dev == prod mirror)

`sources.id=87` (`ryle-expository`, "Expository Thoughts on the Gospels") was acquired with
the CCEL adapter in **author-page mode** (`ccel_author: "ryle"` in ingest/sources.config.json),
which slurped every work on Ryle's CCEL author page into one source row:

- ordinals 1–93: Expository Thoughts on **Matthew** (the intended work)
- ordinals 94–114: *Holiness* chapters I–XXI — **exact duplicate** of source 88
  (`ryle-holiness`, 21 sections, same headings)
- ordinals 115–137: *Upper Room: Being a Few Truths for the Times* chapters I–XXI + 2 notes
  (ch. XV = "THE LORD'S GARDEN" — the reported contamination; it IS Ryle, but the wrong work
  under the wrong source, anchored to Song 4:12 and 42 other stray verses across 24 books)

## Pre-delete safety counts (dev AND prod, both zero)

bookmarks 0, highlights 0, notes 0, library_items 0, reading_progress 0,
section_history_anchors 0, section_embeddings 0, topical_entries 0 on sections ordinal>=94.
section_anchors: 43 (all stray; deleted).

## Applied (single transaction each, dev then prod, identical results)

```sql
DELETE FROM section_anchors WHERE section_id IN
  (SELECT id FROM sections WHERE source_id=87 AND ordinal>=94);          -- DELETE 43
DELETE FROM sections WHERE source_id=87 AND ordinal>=94;                 -- DELETE 44
UPDATE sources SET title='Expository Thoughts on Matthew' WHERE id=87;   -- UPDATE 1
```

Post-check both DBs: 93 sections, 93 anchors, 1 distinct book (40 = Matthew). Title retitled
to the honest "Expository Thoughts on Matthew" (no code or test pins the old title — grep-verified).

## Recurrence prevention

- `ingest/sources.config.json` ryle-expository: `ccel_author: "ryle"` → `ccel_ids: ["ryle/matthew"]`,
  provenance url/edition updated to match. A re-ingest can no longer pull the author page.
- Latent, flagged to ingest lane (NOT fixed today): five other manifest entries still use
  author-page mode (`owen`, `watson`, `flavel`, `edwards`, `vincent`) — there it is the
  declared intent ("*-works" collections), but any future single-work entry must not use
  `ccel_author`. Also `ryle-matthew` (tier 3, never ingested) now points at the same CCEL id
  as ryle-expository — a latent duplicate for the ingest lane to resolve.
- *Upper Room* is restorable anytime via the existing `ryle-upper-room` manifest entry
  (tier 3, never ingested) through the standard loop.

## Flat-store half (found during Song recon, same day)

The contamination ALSO lived in the served flat `embeddings` store: 1,481 served rows keyed
`commentary:ryle-expository:94..137.*` (761 = Holiness duplicates, 720 = Upper Room incl. the
21 `130.*` "Lord's Garden" rows the plan doc flagged). Deleting the sections alone would have
left the served rows live. Verified before delete: Holiness is independently served under its
own slug (`:ryle-holiness:` = 761 served rows, both DBs), so the duplicates carry nothing
unique; Upper Room's only copy goes away until properly ingested via `ryle-upper-room`.

```sql
DELETE FROM embeddings
WHERE source_id LIKE 'commentary:ryle-expository:%'
  AND substring(source_id from 'commentary:ryle-expository:(\d+)\.')::int >= 94;  -- DELETE 1481
```

Post-check both DBs: 559 served rows remain under ryle-expository (ordinals 1–93, Matthew).
No FKs reference `embeddings` (pg_constraint check), so the delete is orphan-free.

## Verification

- Dev + prod post-checks above (in transaction output).
- verse_coverage rebuild deferred to the Song of Solomon job (same session) — one rebuild
  covers both changes; the table is a derived rollup, never hand-edited.
